A fixed-point P controller stores Kp = 1.5 in Q8 format (scaled by 256). What value of u does this C code compute?

int32_t kp_q8 = 384;
int32_t e = 20;
int32_t u = (kp_q8 * e) >> 8;

The PI loop body below runs three times with a constant error of 30. Anti-windup is done by undoing the last integration whenever the output is clamped. What are u and integ after the third pass?

float kp = 2.0f, ki_t = 1.0f, integ = 0.0f, u;
for (int k = 0; k < 3; k++) {
    float e = 30.0f;
    integ += ki_t * e;
    u = kp * e + integ;
    if (u > 100.0f) { u = 100.0f; integ -= ki_t * e; }
}
